  "summary": "Liputa is a style of wearing modern fashion by women in Democratic Republic of the Congo and the Republic of Congo.",
  "description": "Liputa is a style of wearing modern fashion by women in Democratic Republic of the Congo and the Republic of Congo. \"Liputa\" means wearing of colorful materials in style. Usually Congolese women wear fashion of very vibrant colours. Congolese women wear their attire to a marriage ceremony, market, gathering or to a formal party in Liputa style. Mothers who have young children usually use a similar material to carry their baby at the back. This is seen as the norm in the DRC.",
